# Shell scripts must check out with LF endings, everywhere.
#
# Git for Windows defaults to core.autocrlf=true, which rewrites LF to CRLF on
# checkout. A .sh file that lands with CRLF fails at the shebang before a single
# line of logic runs:  bad interpreter: /usr/bin/env bash^M
#
# This matters even though Windows is not a supported target: a WSL user whose
# repo sits on an NTFS mount, or anyone cloning on Windows to read the source,
# hits it otherwise.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Belt and braces for the files that would actually break.
*.sh text eol=lf
